{% videoSection id="9t4g5M3CM3o" title="Why Choose AG Grid Enterprise for your Data Grid" showHeader=true %}
This page provides an overview of the differences between AG Grid Community and Enterprise, when to use each version, and how to access our free trial or purchase a licence.
{% /videoSection %}

## Overview

AG Grid comes in two forms: 

- **AG Grid Community**: Free for everyone, including production use - no license required.
- **AG Grid Enterprise**: Requires a license to use in production. Free to test locally, or request a [trial](#trial-ag-grid-enterprise-for-free) to test in production.

*All Enterprise features are marked with an {% enterpriseIcon /%} in our docs*

### Community Features
- **Data Grid Essentials:** Row and column configurations, sorting, filtering, and pagination.
- **Cell Rendering:** Custom cell rendering using components or plain JavaScript.
- **Themes and Styling:** Pre-built themes and CSS customization.
- **Accessibility Support:** ARIA support and keyboard navigation.
- **Major Frameworks:** Support for React, Angular and Vue, in addition to vanilla JavaScript.

### Enterprise Features

- **Server-Side Row Model:** Efficiently handle large datasets by loading data on-demand from the server.
- **Excel Export:** Advanced export options, including styles and formulas.
- **Pivot Tables & Aggregations:** Built-in pivot and aggregation capabilities for complex data analysis.
- **Range Selection & Charts:** Select and manipulate ranges of data.
- **Integrated Charts:** Create and customize charts directly within the grid.
- **Master/Detail View:** Nested grid views for hierarchical data representation.
- **Row Grouping & Multi-Column Sorting:** Advanced grouping and sorting options for better data organization.
- **Clipboard Operations:** Enhanced copy and paste functionality, including support for Excel-like behaviour.
- **Tool Panels:** Built-in configuration panels for columns, filters, and more.
- **Custom Context Menu & Sidebars:** Additional UI elements for enhanced user interaction and customization.

{% note %}
See the [Pricing](/license-pricing) page for a full feature comparison.
{% /note %}

## Enterprise Bundle 

In addition to AG Grid Enterprise, we also offer an Enterprise Bundle license, which provides access to both [AG Charts](/charts/) Enterprise (our standalone JavaScript Charting Library) and Integrated Enterprise Charts. Without an Enterprise Bundle license, you will only have access to Integrated Community charts. To learn more about the difference between Community Charts and Enterprise Charts, see the [AG Charts Community vs. Enterprise docs](https://www.ag-grid.com/charts/community-vs-enterprise).

## Test AG Grid Enterprise Features

You can test AG Grid Enterprise features locally without a license key, just install the `ag-grid-enterprise` package and import the required modules - you do not need to provide a license key. When you do not have a license key installed then AG Grid Enterprise will display a watermark and an error message in the console.

### Request an Enterprise Bundle Trial license

If you would like to trial AG Grid Enterprise in a production environment, you can request a free trial license key. The trial license key will remove the watermark & console error message, and provide access to both AG Grid and AG Charts Enterprise, as well as dedicated support for the duration of your trial period.

