## Choosing the Right Version

**AG Grid Community** is an excellent choice if you need a robust, feature-rich data grid without the need for advanced enterprise features. It is ideal for developers and organizations looking for a free, open-source solution.

**AG Grid Enterprise** is the preferred option for companies that need advanced functionality, dedicated support, and a flexible licensing model. It is suited for complex applications that demand high performance, extensive customization, and large-scale data handling.

**Enterprise Bundle** is the best choice for organizations that require both AG Grid Enterprise and AG Charts Enterprise, or those who have advanced use-cases for Integrated Charting.

## Support

AG Grid Community relies on community-driven support through GitHub and public forums.

AG Grid Enterprise provides dedicated support via [Zendesk](https://ag-grid.zendesk.com/hc/en-us) with guaranteed response times, bug fixes, and direct access to the AG Grid developers, who handle all support tickets. Support is also available during your free trial period.

## Licensing
Both AG Grid Community and Enterprise are open source, however, **AG Grid Community is available under the MIT license** and **AG Grid Enterprise requires a commercial, EULA license**.

For more information, review our [Licenses on GitHub](https://github.com/ag-grid/ag-grid/tree/latest?tab=License-1-ov-file).

## Pricing

licenses for AG Grid Enterprise are available on a per-developer, per-deployment basis. For more information on pricing, see the [Pricing](/license-pricing) page.

